ers/01-039-what-is-tokenization-and-why-does-it-matter-for-cost-and-con.md — Q39: What is tokenization, and why does it matter for cost and context windows?\n59\t- [ ] answers/01-040-what-is-the-difference-between-prompt-engineering-rag-and-fi.md — Q40: What is the difference between prompt engineering, RAG, and fine-tuning?\n60\t- [ ] answers/01-041-what-are-embeddings-and-how-are-they-used-in-rag.md — Q41: What are embeddings, and how are they used in RAG?\n61\t- [ ] answers/01-042-semantic-search-vs-keyword-search.md — Q42: Semantic search vs keyword search?\n62\t- [ ] answers/01-043-how-do-you-reduce-hallucinations-in-llm-outputs.md — Q43: How do you reduce hallucinations in LLM outputs?\n63\t- [ ] answers/01-044-what-is-the-lost-in-the-middle-problem.md — Q44: What is the \"lost in the middle\" problem?\n64\t- [ ] answers/01-045-when-set-temperature-to-0-vs-higher-values.md — Q45: When set temperature to 0 vs higher values?\n65\t- [ ] answers/01-046-bias-variance-tradeoff.md — Q46: Bias-variance tradeoff?\n66\t- [ ] answers/01-047-overfitting-how-prevent-it.md — Q47: Overfitting — how prevent it?\n67\t- [ ] answers/01-048-imbalanced-datasets-how-handle.md — Q48: Imbalanced datasets — how handle?\n68\t- [ ] validate — run: bash ralph-ai-engineering/validate.sh 01-llm-fundamentals\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f3b2d6e-f3f0-4269-97ea-7056b52ecd18","uuid":"78ec380e-d259-43ad-9105-5000ac270f24","timestamp":"2026-06-16T09:19:03.363Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/ai-engineering/plan.md","content":"# Plan: AI Engineering Interview Prep\n\n## Meta\ncurrent_category: 01-llm-fundamentals\ncategory_name: LLM Fundamentals\ncategory_num: 1\nquestion_range: 1–48\ntask_count: 50\ncreated: 2026-06-16\n\n## Done\n- [x] 0 scaffold — category queue created\n- [x] categories/01-llm-fundamentals.md — category overview: LLM Fundamentals (48 questions)\n- [x] answers/01-001-how-do-llms-work.md — Q