{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01W8j1yaGP4RjVKWYu3gnazr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Completed **Q4: What is the difference between pre-training and fine-tuning?** and wrote `ai-engineering/answers/01-004-what-is-the-difference-between-pre-training-and-fine-tuning.md`.\n\nThe answer covers:\n- **Pre-training** — next-token prediction on 1–15T tokens, trains all weights from scratch, produces a base model (knowledge + language ability, but not instruction-following)\n- **SFT** — fine-tunes on 10K–1M curated instruction-response pairs to teach format and instruction adherence  \n- **RLHF vs DPO** — RLHF uses PPO + a reward model; DPO skips the reward model and directly optimizes on preference pairs (now dominant in 2026: Llama-3, Mistral-Instruct, Qwen)\n- **LoRA/QLoRA** — parameter-efficient fine-tuning that trains <1% of weights, enabling a 70B fine-tune on a single A100\n- **Critical tradeoff** — fine-tuning changes *behavior*, not *knowledge*; don't use it to inject facts (use RAG instead)\n- 3-pitfall section targeting common screening mistakes, 3 related question cross-links\n\nNext unchecked plan item: **Q5: Explain context windows and their limitations.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":83918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":342,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f3b2d6e-f3f0-4269-97ea-7056b52ecd18","uuid":"0e5969ef-3204-47de-b8eb-9bb10bd170a0"}
